{"step_index":307,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T09:56:44Z","content":"Great! The gRPC server is up and running:\n\n```\n2026-09-12 15:24:44 [info] gRPC Actuator server listening on 50051\n```\n\n### Next steps for you\n\n1. **Test the server (optional)**  \n   You can open another terminal, keep the virtual environment active, and run a simple client script to verify it responds. For example:\n\n   ```bat\n   (venv) C:\\hackbattle>python - <<EOF\n   import grpc\n   from common.proto import actuator_pb2_grpc as act_grpc, actuator_pb2 as act_pb\n   channel = grpc.insecure_channel('localhost:50051')\n   stub = act_grpc.ActuatorStub(channel)\n   request = act_pb.ActuateRequest(type=act_pb.ActuationType.CLICK, x=100, y=200, text=\"\")\n   try:\n       response = stub.Execute(request)\n       print(\"Response:\", response)\n   except grpc.RpcError as e:\n       print(\"RPC error:\", e)\n   EOF\n   ```\n\n   You should see a `UNIMPLEMENTED` response (the server stub raises `NotImplementedError` by design). That’s expected and confirms communication works.\n\n2. **Run the full pipeline** (once you’re ready to see the end‑to‑end flow)\n\n   ```bat\n   (venv) C:\\hackbattle>python run_pipeline.py\n   ```\n\n   This will:\n   - Capture screen frames,\n   - Publish UI elements,\n   - Detect drift via the BE‑2 memory engine,\n   - Invoke the gRPC actuator to click or drag as needed.\n\n3. **Implement the actuator logic** (optional)  \n   The `ActuatorServicer.Execute` method in `app/grpc_server/server.py` currently raises `NotImplementedError`. Replace that with actual mouse/keyboard actions (using `pyautogui`, `pynput`, etc.) when you’re ready to make the system interactive.\n\nLet me know if you’d like to:\n- Add the actual actuation implementation,\n- Verify the pipeline output,\n- Or anything else you’d like to explore. 🚀"}
